  "title": "Exact Hurwitz Stability of Independence Polynomials for All Trees on 21 Vertices",
  "batch_label": "63",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every finite simple tree T on exactly 21 vertices, every zero of its independence polynomial I(T,z) has strictly negative real part. Hence every such polynomial is stable in the frozen source's closed-left-half-plane sense. The exhaustive census contains exactly 2,144,505 unlabeled isomorphism classes; each has a regular exact Routh table with strictly positive first column, and there are no unstable or singular classes.",
